1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,700
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,070
How do you do?

3
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,300
Hello.

4
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,300
I'm Ralph Riley.

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,900
I'm Richard Stewart, and this is my wife, Marilyn.

6
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:13,848
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:14,400
Likewise, Mr. Riley.

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:19,300
Please, sit down. What can I do for you?

9
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,500
We'd like to discuss a mortgage.

10
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,500
For a house.

11
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,700
Fine. Are you buying a house

12
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,500
or are you refinancing your present home?

13
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,400
We're planning to buy a house.

14
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,771
And we'd like to find out about a mortgage.

15
00:00:30,771 --> 00:00:32,623
We are customers of the bank.

16
00:00:32,623 --> 00:00:35,460
As a matter of fact, my whole family banks here.

17
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:38,400
I have some questions to ask.

18
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,800
Do you own your house or do you rent?

19
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:41,963
Neither.

20
00:00:41,963 --> 00:00:46,800
We live with my parents, Dr. and Mrs. Philip Stewart.

21
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,000
And how old are you?

22
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:49,400
I'm twenty-nine.

23
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,100
I'm thirty.

24
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:54,684
And, Mr. Stewart, what is your occupation?

25
00:00:54,684 --> 00:00:56,300
I'm a freelance photographer.

26
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,921
And, Mrs. Stewart, are you working?

27
00:00:57,921 --> 00:01:01,700
Yes. I'm a designer, and I work in a boutique.

28
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,699
Did you bring any savings or salary information?

29
00:01:03,699 --> 00:01:04,893
Last year's tax forms?

30
00:01:04,893 --> 00:01:12,700
Yes. Here they are.

31
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,900
OK. What ... what kind of house did you have in mind?

32
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:16,100
We're talking about buying

33
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:18,300
a two-bedroom house in Mount Kisco.

34
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:24,300
Here are the financial details on the house.

35
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:25,300
Thank you.

36
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:26,100
Are you prepared to make a ten-percent down payment?

37
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:28,600
Yes, we are.

38
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,019
Payments over thirty years?

39
00:01:30,019 --> 00:01:33,300
Yes.

40
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,800
Do you think we can get a loan?

41
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:40,400
Well, it depends. Do you own any other property?

42
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,400
Any stocks or bonds?

43
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,337
No.

44
00:01:45,337 --> 00:01:50,200
I see. Then you don't have any collateral.

45
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,100
Perhaps you could get a guarantor--

46
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:54,600
someone to sign for the loan for you.

47
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,491
Why is that necessary?

48
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:57,781
Since you don't have enough income,

49
00:01:57,781 --> 00:01:59,796
and you don't already own any property,

50
00:01:59,796 --> 00:02:00,800
the bank needs to be sure

51
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,880
you can pay the mortgage every month.

52
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:04,800
A guarantor is responsible for the loan

53
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:06,600
if you can't make the payments.

54
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:13,800
I see. Well, the idea of buying a house is exciting.

55
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:17,100
Thank you, Mr. Riley. We'll read this over carefully.

56
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,170
Thank you.

57
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:18,700
Good-bye. Thanks.

58
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:22,800
Good-bye. And hope to see you soon.

59
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,100
I hope so, too.

60
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,400
Take care.

61
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:43,582
Good-bye.

62
00:02:43,582 --> 00:02:44,442
It all sounded so easy

63
00:02:44,442 --> 00:02:48,100
until they mentioned needing collateral or a guarantor.

64
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:51,500
We have no collateral.

65
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,200
And I don't think it's a good idea

66
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:55,400
to ask Dad to sign as a guarantor.

67
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,300
I don't feel right about it.

68
00:02:57,300 --> 00:03:11,870
I understand your feelings about it, Richard.

69
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:19,600
We can get a loan from the bank

70
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:20,700
[03:25.43]if we can put up some collateral.

71
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,800
And we don't own anything to use as collateral.

72
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:28,500
Or someone can sign with us as a guarantor.

73
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,300
Why don't you speak to Dad?

74
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:35,400
No. If we buy a house, I want to be able to handle it alone.

75
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,500
Everybody needs help sometimes, Richard.

76
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,500
I understand Richard's feelings about it, Ellen.

77
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,600
In two or three months, I'll have an advance on my book

78
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,800
and be able to put more money down.

79
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:48,700
What about the house in Mount Kisco?

80
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,795
Somebody else'll buy it by then.

81
00:03:50,795 --> 00:03:53,300
Then there'll be other houses, Marilyn.

82
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:57,600
Richard has a point. You're just beginning to look. Richard

83
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,800
We're in no great rush. It's true.

84
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,900
This has been a great learning experience for us, Marilyn.

85
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,019
Talking to the real-estate agent.

86
00:04:03,019 --> 00:04:05,100
Looking at the houses.

87
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:09,300
Talking to the loan officer at the bank.

88
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,946
It has been a learning experience. That's true.

89
00:04:10,946 --> 00:04:13,700
I think you're doing the right thing. Taking your time.

90
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:17,100
Looking around. Especially with a purchase of this kind.

91
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,600
You're talking about a lot of money.

92
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:23,400
We'll call Mrs. Martinelli and tell her to keep looking for us.

93
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:28,500
And I'll call Mr. Riley at the bank

94
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:28,800
and tell him we'll see him in a couple of months.

95
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,000
And if you ever need Dad or me to help you ...

96
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,400
We know.

97
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,500
You know we'll be there for you.

98
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:37,500
It's a Stewart tradition. We're a family.
